{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":21,"result":{"data":{"brief":{"briefId":"brief-638a6b63-880d-4d3d-a8a7-fec1de8f273f","title":"API REV 004 Studio exact identity brief","status":"in_review","latestBindingId":"c048d150-abd5-4827-881e-8ff21667f9e3","latestRunId":"brief_studio_team_4f4a2a03ea094345bf53080b0f896c33","latestBindingStatus":"ATTACHED","lastErrorMessage":null,"createdAt":"2026-08-22T12:21:03.257Z","updatedAt":"2026-08-22T12:22:35.313Z","approvedAt":null,"rejectedAt":null,"artifacts":[{"briefId":"brief-638a6b63-880d-4d3d-a8a7-fec1de8f273f","artifactKind":"researcher","publicationKind":"research","revisionId":"cb0be036-c6b4-4a78-a096-ed12fc8b1042","path":"/private/tmp/api-rev004-studio.xkprY3/applications/bundle-app__brief-studio__dff2993a20fe475cc984604995d2289c03130e4d46e5d81db3c2ac2211b740f7/runtime/brief-studio/research.md","description":"Concise research checkpoint for the exact identity brief.","body":"# API REV 004 Studio exact identity brief — research checkpoint\n\n## Key findings\n- The brief title is the only supplied source context; the central requirement is exact identity, not a broad brand exploration.\n- “API REV 004 Studio” should be treated as the canonical name, preserving capitalization, spacing, and the three-part structure exactly.\n- “exact identity” implies a reviewable identity spec: approved name treatment, concise positioning, voice, visual direction, and explicit exclusions.\n- The checkpoint should distinguish confirmed facts (the title) from proposed identity decisions so reviewers can approve or revise them cleanly.\n- A compact brief is preferable: one central promise, a small set of identity principles, and concrete acceptance criteria.\n\n## Risks or open questions\n- No product description, audience, market, geography, or existing visual references were provided.\n- “API REV 004” could be a project/version code or an outward-facing brand element; its public display role needs confirmation.\n- Exact logo, color, typography, and usage rules cannot be finalized without stakeholder/source validation.\n\n## Recommendations or next steps\n- Draft the identity around precision, technical fluency, and studio craft while labeling these as working hypotheses.\n- Make the canonical lockup “API REV 004 Studio” and define any shortened form only as a secondary usage.\n- Include a reviewer checklist covering naming, audience, promise, tone, visual system, and prohibited variants.\n","producerMemberAddress":"/researcher","updatedAt":"2026-08-22T12:21:48.330Z"},{"briefId":"brief-638a6b63-880d-4d3d-a8a7-fec1de8f273f","artifactKind":"writer","publicationKind":"final","revisionId":"28f39da2-3405-41b5-9cca-58d2d3e85b7f","path":"/private/tmp/api-rev004-studio.xkprY3/applications/bundle-app__brief-studio__dff2993a20fe475cc984604995d2289c03130e4d46e5d81db3c2ac2211b740f7/runtime/brief-studio/final-brief.md","description":"Concise reviewable identity brief for API REV 004 Studio.","body":"# API REV 004 Studio — Identity Brief\n\n**Recommendation summary**\n\nAdopt **“API REV 004 Studio”** as the canonical identity treatment, preserving its capitalization, spacing, and three-part structure exactly. Build a compact identity around a clear, exacting, technically fluent studio character. The following positioning, voice, and visual direction are working hypotheses—not validated brand decisions—because no audience, product description, market context, or visual references were supplied.\n\n**Key evidence**\n\n- **Confirmed naming:** The supplied title is the only firm source context; therefore, the exact name treatment is the strongest approved direction.\n- **Positioning hypothesis:** A precision-led studio that turns complex systems, revisions, or technical work into clear, crafted outcomes.\n- **Voice:** Direct, calm, specific, and confident. Prefer plain language, useful detail, and deliberate restraint over hype, jargon, or exaggerated claims.\n- **Visual direction:** Structured and editorial; use disciplined spacing, modular layouts, strong hierarchy, and a restrained technical sensibility. Let craft and clarity lead rather than decorative futurism.\n- **Identity principle:** Every touchpoint should feel intentional, legible, and revision-aware—precise enough for technical audiences, but accessible to non-specialists.\n- **Exclusions:** Do not introduce unapproved shortened names, alternate capitalization, generic “AI/tech” visual clichés, noisy gradients, gratuitous code imagery, or claims that imply a defined product or audience.\n\n**Risks or cautions**\n\n- “API REV 004” may be an internal project/version code rather than a public-facing brand element; confirm its display role before finalizing.\n- Logo construction, color palette, typography, spacing, and accessibility rules remain undefined and require stakeholder/source validation.\n- Precision, technical fluency, and studio craft are hypotheses inferred from the name and brief—not evidence-based audience insights.\n- Avoid presenting this checkpoint as a final brand system until the audience, offer, and competitive context are known.\n\n**Next actions**\n\n- Confirm whether **“API REV 004 Studio”** is the public-facing canonical name and whether a secondary short form is permitted.\n- Validate the intended audience, offer, market context, and any existing visual references.\n- Approve or revise the positioning and voice hypotheses.\n- Develop two or three visual routes, then select and document the logo, color, type, layout, and usage rules.\n- Run a reviewer checklist for name fidelity, promise, tone, visual coherence, accessibility, and prohibited variants.\n","producerMemberAddress":"/writer","updatedAt":"2026-08-22T12:22:35.313Z"}],"reviewNotes":[]}}}}
